# `existential-escape` (Type System ch. 5, "Existentials are dictionaries"): an `any ^Show`
# given to `Same`'s bare `a` is unpacked into a fresh rigid type, which `Same` hands back,
# so the hidden type would leave the existential; `Show v` gives a `Text` and is fine, as
# is pushing an existential into an array of them, whose `a` is already one.
Same: fn a -> a
fn Same x = x

Leak: fn (any ^Show) -> Text
fn Leak v:
    let w = Same v
    "{Show v} {Len (Push [[v]], v)}"
